menu "Mosaico application power policy"
    config MOSAICO_STANDBY_AUTO_LIGHT_SLEEP
        bool "Automatically use validated light sleep while Mosaico is locked"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31 && PM_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            Enable the RAM-only normal locked-screen policy. Runtime still requires
            the complete validated safe sleep profile, UART recovery, fixed 160 MHz,
            a stable locked display, no OTA or boot-health work, and radio inactivity.
            Awake/OTA pause the policy; explicit debug standby-sleep off disables it
            until auto CONFIRM or reboot. No NVS setting is written.
    config MOSAICO_LVGL_MONOTONIC_TICK
        bool "Use the Mosaico monotonic LVGL tick with a 1000 ms port timer"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
        default n
        help
            Use LVGL's public tick callback with the monotonic ESP timer. Capture a
            startup offset under the LVGL mutex to preserve tick continuity. The
            existing port tick timer runs every 1000 ms; no new task or timer is
            created. Touch polling, LVGL handler deadlines, animation, main-loop
            and wireless scheduling are unchanged. Disabled keeps the 10 ms tick.
endmenu
